    "answer": {
      "short": "One possible pairing is $(1,12),\\ (2,7),\\ (3,8),\\ (4,9),\\ (5,10),\\ (6,11)$.\n\nThe differences are $11$ and $5$, both odd primes.",
      "worked": "An odd difference requires pairing an odd number with an even number. One possible pairing is\n$$\\begin{aligned}(1,12),\\ (2,7),\\ (3,8),\\\\(4,9),\\ (5,10),\\ (6,11).\\end{aligned}$$\nCheck the differences:\n$$\\begin{align*}12-1&=11\\\\7-2&=5\\\\8-3&=5\\\\9-4&=5\\\\10-5&=5\\\\11-6&=5\\end{align*}$$\nBoth $5$ and $11$ are odd primes, and every number from $1$ to $12$ occurs exactly once.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 100
